# Desktop polish Windows v0.2.2 release
Workstream-ID: lea-22
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/22
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed release follow-through for completed desktop presentation work
Status: DONE
Milestone: Deliver the completed desktop improvements in a verified Windows release
Dependencies: lea-15, lea-17, lea-18, lea-19, lea-20, lea-21

## Purpose
Publish the completed desktop logs, hover help, live outcome counters and fixed
toolbar as Windows v0.2.2. Keep the concise illustrated README, source launcher
and packaged capabilities aligned without replacing private setup or controlling
an independently running application.

## Tasks
- [x] Verify publication authority, repository identity, prior releases and unused version.
- [x] Establish that the existing source launcher runs the checkout, not a downloaded EXE.
- [x] Review the exact public payload and align version, release notes and usage guides.
- [x] Run source release gates without using real browser or applicant data.
- [x] Commit/push only reviewed files with repository-local attribution and required trailers.
- [x] Publish the matching tag through the existing qualification-gated Windows pipeline.
- [x] Download and verify hosted assets, exact source identity and all bundled file hashes.
- [x] Install into a new local version directory and exercise frozen GUI/CLI offline.
- [x] Verify the existing source launcher and preservation of private setup and earlier releases.
- [x] Reconcile the issue, Project status and persistent backlink.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Package metadata, tag, hosted run and downloaded manifest identify one exact release source.
- [x] The downloadable desktop includes readable colored logs, two-line hover help, live counters and the fixed toolbar.
- [x] README media and usage guides distinguish the new release from unchanged older binaries.
- [x] The installed actual asset passes the existing frozen offline checks.
- [x] The source launcher keeps its existing command and configured workspace without reinitialization.
- [x] Private inputs, authentication, runtime data, continuity and unrelated work are not published.
- [x] Earlier release assets and existing installations are preserved; no running GUI is driven or restarted.
- [x] Publication and offline qualification are not presented as live-site, clean-machine or human acceptance.
- [x] One repository issue, one correctly staged Project item and a durable backlink represent this workstream.

## Completion evidence
Initial read-back verified the public repository, owner access and remote main.
The prior release inventory contains v0.2.0 and v0.2.1; the v0.2.2 tag is absent.
The configured source launcher directly invokes the checkout's existing Python,
GUI entrypoint and configuration. It does not select or download release assets.
Preservation baselines cover existing public changes, selected private-file
metadata, native preference metadata, all twenty-one tracking mappings and empty
staging. Package metadata is v0.2.2, and the concise README, affected guides,
bundled tutorial and first-run instructions match the completed desktop features.
The corrected full source gate passes Ruff, Black (117 files), mypy (72 source
files) and all 772 tests with native exit zero. The initial two order-dependent
test failures and their isolated-import fix are retained in the log.
The reviewed 56-file source is published at
d06cf742fa7ce6b63267cf5efb5033504a713db8 with matching annotated tag v0.2.2,
repository-local attribution and both required session trailers. Canonical
GitHub tree read-back independently matches every reviewed blob. Exact push
runs 42682056610 (main) and 42682056827 (tag) both pass qualification; only
the version-tag run publishes. The hosted release notes match the reviewed
versioned notes, and the latest stable release is v0.2.2:
https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/releases/tag/v0.2.2

All three actual downloaded assets match hosted sizes/digests and SHA256SUMS.
The manifest identifies that exact source and version. ZIP safety/inventory
and all 450 extracted file sizes/hashes are verified before and after placement.
The 114,579,088-byte ZIP has SHA256
a46ceddf5924295892e0c09575a51c6aad6de4d1d75aef62bb64702136ff409e.
The bundle is installed side by side in a new 0.2.2 version directory.
Eight existing frozen offline checks pass with native exit zero: version,
help, init, stats, test-form, CSV/XLSX exports and actual GUI render/driver/
sibling-child integration. The installed CLI separately reports 0.2.2;
the bundled tutorial matches the reviewed source and contains 21 topics.

The unchanged source-launcher check still passes without opening a GUI or
starting automation. Selected original-input/native preference metadata,
all fifteen reviewed media hashes, earlier installed public entrypoints,
both older hosted releases/assets and their tag refs remain unchanged.
No real workspace contents or user processes are used as test fixtures.
These are installed-asset offline checks, not live LinkedIn, clean-machine
or human visual acceptance. Scoped issue/Project/backlink completion is
independently reconciled; its settled no-churn receipt is retained separately.
Subsequent tracking-only commits do not move the immutable release tag.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-10: Started the separately authorized release follow-through. Preserve
